IMPORT prelude

-- Institute of Technical Education Act 1992 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person or business outside the Institute:
-- fees and the validation of late-payment charges (ss 6(1)(i), 6A), protection of the Institute's people from suit (s 24), the
-- symbol and certificate-title offences (ss 35, 36), compulsory insurance of trainees (s 37), work-injury cover during training
-- (s 38), returns from employers and their confidentiality (s 39), obstruction (s 40), prosecution (ss 41, 42), officers of a
-- body corporate (s 43), and vacation of office by a Board member (s 9).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation
-- (version in force from 1/7/2026), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ITEA1992.txt. The latest amendment annotated is
-- Act 17 of 2026 (Skills and Workforce Development Agency Act 2026), in force 1 July 2026, which adds s 5(c). The legislative
-- history lists Act 4 of 2008 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008) with "Commencement : 1 April 2024".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0175 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED accordingly. Not encoded: the Institute's establishment, seal, functions and powers other
-- than fees (ss 3-6), the Board's constitution and procedure other than s 9 (ss 7, 8, 10-15), the 1992 transfer from the
-- Vocational and Industrial Training Board (ss 16-19, 45), staff (ss 22, 23), finance (ss 26-29), and regulations (s 44). No
-- regulations made under s 44 were retrieved, so actual fees, late charges, apprenticeship rules and insurance terms are unknown.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Institute of Technical Education Act 1992 -- the public`

§§ `6(1)(i) and 6A -- fees and late-payment charges`

-- s 6(1)(i): the Institute may "levy and collect -- (i) such fees, rates or charges for training and other services, use of
-- facilities and conduct of activities; and (ii) such charges for the late payment thereof, as the Institute may consider
-- expedient" [Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024].
-- s 6A: "Every amount collected before the date of commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008 as, or
-- purportedly as, a charge for the late payment of any fee, rate or charge referred to in section 6(i) shall be deemed to be and
-- always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie ... in respect of any such collection."
-- The legislative history gives that Act's commencement as 1 April 2024 (passed 22 January 2008). Dates are YYYYMMDD numbers.
GIVEN `the date of collection` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a claim over the late-payment charge is barred by s 6A` IF
    `the date of collection` LESS THAN 20240401

§§ `24 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 24: "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie against any member or any employee of the Institute or other person acting
-- under the direction of the Institute for anything which is in good faith done or intended to be done in the execution or
-- purported execution of this Act." The protection is of the individual; the Institute itself is not named (s 3(a): it may be
-- sued).
GIVEN `is a member, employee or person acting under the Institute's direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted in the execution or purported execution of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a suit lies against the individual` IF
    NOT (    `is a member, employee or person acting under the Institute's direction`
         AND `acted in good faith`
         AND `acted in the execution or purported execution of the Act`)

§§ `35 and 36 -- the symbol and the titles of certificates`

-- s 35(2): "Any person or body corporate who uses a symbol, design or representation identical with that of the Institute or
-- which so resembles [it] as to deceive or cause confusion or to be likely to deceive or cause confusion" -- fine up to $2,000.
-- s 36(2): "Any person who issues or uses, or causes or permits the use of, titles of certificates or other qualifications
-- IDENTICAL with those of the Institute" -- fine up to $2,000. Section 36 has no resemblance limb.
GIVEN `uses the symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `the symbol is identical` IS A BOOLEAN, `the resemblance is likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use of the symbol is an offence` IF
    `uses the symbol` AND (`the symbol is identical` OR `the resemblance is likely to deceive or confuse`)

GIVEN `issues, uses, or causes or permits the use of the title` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the title is identical` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the title is confusingly similar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use of the title is an offence` IF
    `issues, uses, or causes or permits the use of the title` AND `the title is identical`

§§ `37 -- compulsory insurance`

-- s 37: the Institute "may require any person who attends any course or avails himself or herself of any facility provided or
-- approved by the Institute under this Act to be insured against personal injuries and loss of life."
GIVEN `attends a course` IS A BOOLEAN, `uses a facility` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is provided or approved by the Institute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Institute may require the person to be insured` IF
    (`attends a course` OR `uses a facility`) AND `it is provided or approved by the Institute`

§§ `38 -- accidents to employees during training`

-- s 38(2): for the Work Injury Compensation Act 2019, "any act done by an employee for the purposes of and in connection with his
-- or her training referred to in subsection (1) is, if it is not done for the purposes of and in connection with his or her
-- employer's trade or business, deemed to be so done." Subsection (1): employees "who attend courses or avail themselves of the
-- facilities provided or approved by the Institute".
GIVEN `is an employee under the Work Injury Compensation Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the training is provided or approved by the Institute` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the act was for and in connection with the training` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the act was for and in connection with the employer's business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act counts as done for the employer's business` IF
        `the act was for and in connection with the employer's business`
    OR  (    `is an employee under the Work Injury Compensation Act`
         AND `the training is provided or approved by the Institute`
         AND `the act was for and in connection with the training`)

§§ `39 -- returns from employers`

-- s 39(1): the Chief Executive Officer "may require employers in commerce or industry to furnish such returns and other
-- information and to keep such records and produce them for examination". s 2: "commerce or industry" includes "any trade,
-- manufacturing or service industry, business or other related activity".
GIVEN `is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN, `is in commerce or industry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Chief Executive Officer may require returns from it` IF
    `is an employer` AND `is in commerce or industry`

-- s 39(2): without the employer's consent, the returns and information "must not ... be disclosed otherwise than to -- (a) the
-- Institute or a committee appointed by the Institute; (b) an officer of the Institute or of the committee; or (c) any person
-- entitled to take part in the proceedings of the Institute."
-- s 39(3): (2) does not apply to (a) a summary of returns from "a number of employers" framed so that no individual business can
-- be identified; or (b) disclosure "for the purposes of any legal proceedings pursuant to this Act or any criminal proceedings,
-- whether pursuant to this Act or not, or for the purposes of any report of those proceedings".
-- Civil proceedings under another law are NOT in the exception.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the Institute or its committee`
    `an officer of the Institute or committee`
    `a person entitled to take part in the Institute's proceedings`
    `another government agency`
    `a competitor`
    `the press`

DECLARE Occasion IS ONE OF
    `no proceedings`
    `legal proceedings under this Act`
    `criminal proceedings under another law`
    `civil proceedings under another law`
    `a report of proceedings under this Act or criminal proceedings`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient is inside the Institute` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `the Institute or its committee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an officer of the Institute or committee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person entitled to take part in the Institute's proceedings` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the occasion` IS A Occasion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occasion is excepted` IF
    CONSIDER `the occasion`
    WHEN `legal proceedings under this Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `criminal proceedings under another law` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a report of proceedings under this Act or criminal proceedings` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `the occasion` IS A Occasion, `the employer consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is an anonymised summary from a number of employers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is permitted` IF
        `the employer consented`
    OR  `the recipient is inside the Institute` `the recipient`
    OR  `it is an anonymised summary from a number of employers`
    OR  `the occasion is excepted` `the occasion`

-- s 39(6)(c): disclosing "any information in contravention of subsection (2)" is an offence.
GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `the occasion` IS A Occasion, `the employer consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is an anonymised summary from a number of employers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
    NOT `the disclosure is permitted` `the recipient` `the occasion` `the employer consented` `it is an anonymised summary from a number of employers`

-- s 39(6)(a): "knowingly or recklessly furnishes ... any return or other information which is false in a material particular".
GIVEN `the return is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew` IS A BOOLEAN, `was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `furnishing the false return is an offence` IF
    `the return is false in a material particular` AND (`knew` OR `was reckless`)

§§ `35, 36, 39(5), 39(6) and 40 -- the penalties`

-- s 39(5): failing to comply with a requirement under (1) -- "a fine not exceeding $1,000 and, in the case of a second or
-- subsequent conviction, to a fine not exceeding $2,000". s 39(6) (false return, false record entry, unlawful disclosure), s 40
-- (obstructing an officer, employee or agent of the Institute), s 35 and s 36: a fine not exceeding $2,000. No offence in the Act
-- carries imprisonment.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `using the Institute's symbol`
    `using an identical certificate title`
    `failing to furnish a return`
    `furnishing a false return`
    `making a false entry in a record`
    `disclosing returns unlawfully`
    `obstructing an officer of the Institute`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `previous convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to furnish a return` THEN
        IF `previous convictions` GREATER THAN 0 THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    OTHERWISE 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is available` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `41, 42 and 43 -- prosecution and officers of a body corporate`

-- s 42: "No prosecution ... may be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor." s 41: proceedings "may,
-- with the authorisation of the Public Prosecutor, be conducted by an employee of the Institute."
GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor consented or instituted it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `the Public Prosecutor consented or instituted it`

GIVEN `is an employee of the Institute` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Public Prosecutor authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee may conduct the prosecution` IF
    `is an employee of the Institute` AND `the Public Prosecutor authorised it`

-- s 43: where a body corporate commits an offence "with the consent or connivance of, or to be attributable to any act or default
-- on the part of, any director, manager, secretary or other similar officer ... or any person who was purporting to act in any
-- such capacity, he or she, as well as the body corporate, shall be guilty of that offence".
GIVEN `the body corporate committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a director, manager, secretary or similar officer, or purported to act as one` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the offence is attributable to the officer's act or default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the body corporate committed the offence`
    AND `is a director, manager, secretary or similar officer, or purported to act as one`
    AND (`consented or connived` OR `the offence is attributable to the officer's act or default`)

§§ `9 -- vacation of office by a Board member`

-- s 9: the office is vacated if the member "(a) becomes mentally disordered and incapable of managing himself or herself or his or
-- her affairs; (b) is adjudicated a bankrupt; (c) is convicted of an offence involving dishonesty or fraud; (d) fails to attend,
-- without leave of the Board, 3 consecutive meetings of the Board; or (e) resigns from his or her office."
GIVEN `mentally disordered and incapable` IS A BOOLEAN, `adjudicated bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `convicted of an offence involving dishonesty or fraud` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consecutive meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER, `resigned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member's office is vacated` IF
        `mentally disordered and incapable`
    OR  `adjudicated bankrupt`
    OR  `convicted of an offence involving dishonesty or fraud`
    OR  `consecutive meetings missed without leave` AT LEAST 3
    OR  `resigned`
